Z||000000||pherder||08-10-2000||12:17 PM||||To correct a wiring problem that keeps escaping me ... I have to drop out (15th time either removing or installing) the engine/transaxle assembly.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  My scanner shows that my MAP is @ reference voltage and doesn't move (sets code 33) and my Intake Air Temperature is at 304 degrees F.  (Yes it is hot in Kansas, but not THAT HOT!!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>What worries me is I just went out to the shop and removed/disconnected everything on the top of the engine to include the computer wiring from inside the car in about 15 minutes.  All that is left to remove before dropping the assembly is the tires,  the radiator hoses, the struts, the e-brake connection,  the brake lines, and, of course, the mounting bolts for the cradle.<P>So, less than an hour total, I can have the engine sitting on a roll around cart and out of the car.  <P>I know practice makes perfect but I don't want to be this perfect!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Latest thoughts for my three project 88 Fieros are to put the HO Quad 4 assembly in the 88 Formula and have a fun, run around car that can me autocrossed (and get great fuel mileage!)(Yes, I know it would be in FP but I could be class champion here in the Wichita area since there isn't any others!!)  Put the TPI V8 in the 88 Coupe and put the ARTERO body kit on it and put a stock (1st overbore that needs to be assembled) 2.8 into the 88 GT.<P>Paul<BR>------------------<BR>Sedgwick, KS<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT ... All Fiero stuff (including V8 install and ARTERO body kit) for sale ... $15,000 takes all three cars and all the parts I have!!!<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 08-10-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||pherder||08-10-2000||02:28 PM||||20 minutues after going back into the shop, the engine is on the roll around and out from under the 88 Coupe.<P>Let's see ... 15 plus 20 euqals 35 minutes from a running car to the engine/transaxle assembly sitting next to it.  Only one thing I didn't have to do is drain the coolant.  I haven't put any in until I am SURE I will not have to drain it.<P>Paul<P>------------------<BR>Sedgwick, KS<BR>88 Coupe, 88 Formula, 88 GT ... All Fiero stuff (including V8 install and ARTERO body kit) for sale ... $15,000 takes all three cars and all the parts I have!!!||||reg||6
